From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:57:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Enable the accelerometer and
 gyroscope

The J604 ADT has /arm-io/aop/iop-aop-nub/accel and gyro, each with the
three calibration containers aop_motion sends (accel-range-intr-cal,
accel-nominal-extr-cal, accel-range-extr-cal and the gyro- ones; one
location-0 entry each), and on 1.606 the AOP firmware announces both
services (accel.N.auto and gyro.N.auto, unbound).

Enable both children. With a bootloader that copies the calibration
(apple,range-intrinsic-cal and the two extrinsic properties) aop_motion
binds and registers aop-sensors-accel and aop-sensors-gyro at 50 Hz;
without it the driver leaves the sensors off and does not bind, so this
is safe before the bootloader change is installed.

The accelerometer is labelled accel-base: on a clamshell laptop it is in
the base, which tells iio-sensor-proxy not to turn the screen with it.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 9609db5a89..e84afe2cb2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -750,6 +750,20 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * The motion sensor: ADT /arm-io/aop/iop-aop-nub/accel and gyro, each with
+ * its range-intr-cal, nominal-extr-cal and range-extr-cal containers, which
+ * the bootloader copies into these nodes. It sits in the base, not the lid.
+ */
+&aop_accel {
+	label = "accel-base";
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&aop_gyro {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &aop_dart {
 	status = "okay"; /* DTV-AUD-4 */
 };
